   "evidence": "Basic.lean:867 `toPDCode := PDCode.kink` with no accompanying lemma (only `crossingSign_positiveKink` at 881). Every sibling definition has one: `reverse_toPDCode` (501), `mirror_toPDCode` (531), `relabel_toPDCode` (574), `mirror_toOrientedPDCode` (667), `relabel_toOrientedPDCode` (698), `reverse_toOrientedPDCode` (744). Non-exposure is confirmed by `Grid/Unknot/Basic.lean:95-97` (\"The body of `unknot` is deliberately not exposed, so the projection lemmas below are written `(rfl)`\") and by this PR itself having to reprove `kink_edgePair_apply` (Kauffman.lean:414-420) from `kink_edgePair_val` rather than `simp [kink]`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/KnotTheory/PDCode/Basic.lean",
   "fix": "Add `@[simp] theorem positiveKink_toPDCode : positiveKink.toPDCode = PDCode.kink := (rfl)`, plus `@[simp] theorem positiveKink_orientation (h : Fin (4 * 1)) : positiveKink.orientation h = decide (h = 1 \u2228 h = 2) := (rfl)` and `@[simp] theorem positiveKink_crossinglessComponents : positiveKink.crossinglessComponents = 0 := (rfl)`, using `(rfl)` per the repo convention so no defeq is exported.",
   "issue": "`positiveKink` has no projection lemmas: nothing exposes `toPDCode = PDCode.kink`, `orientation`, or `crossinglessComponents`. Since bodies are not `@[expose]`d, a downstream module knows only `crossingSign_positiveKink` and cannot derive `positiveKink.halfEdge = 1`, `positiveKink.overPair i = true`, or any `kink_*` fact about it \u2014 the PR's stated deliverable (positiveKink is kink plus orientation) is not visible in the API.",
